    "title": "San Jose works to move people at Columbus Park encampment into housing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "NBC Bay Area\nwebsite\nSan Jose\nSan Jose works to move people at Columbus Park encampment into housing\nBy Robert Handa,\n2 hours agoSlowly but surely the city of San Jose is cleaning up its largest homeless encampment at Columbus Park and moving more people into converted motel rooms. On Wednesday, Fernando Alcantara moved into the Casa Linda Motel – one of only about two dozen people so far. Alcantara, an electrician by trade, lived at Columbus Park for two years. He likes his new room better.",
